# Build-context exclusions for the SIGNER image only.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# The signer builds from the repository ROOT (see docker-compose.yml) so it can
# share tx_verify.py and execution_rails.py with the pipeline instead of
# carrying second copies that drift. A root context means Docker would
# otherwise apply the ROOT .dockerignore -- which excludes signer_service/
# entirely, because the WEB image must never contain the signing key. Applied
# to this build that exclusion removes the signer's own source and the build
# fails at COPY.
#
# BuildKit reads <dockerfile-path>.dockerignore in preference to the context
# root's, so this file scopes the rules correctly per image. BuildKit is the
# default builder in Docker Desktop; if a build ever reports that
# signer_service/ is missing, the legacy builder is in use -- set
# DOCKER_BUILDKIT=1.
#
# The web image's protection is unaffected: the root .dockerignore still
# applies to the web build, so signer_service/ and every credential pattern
# stay out of it.

# Secrets never enter any image layer. The signer receives these at RUNTIME
# through env_file in docker-compose.
.env
*.env
!.env.example
*credential*
*credentials*
*secret*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*

# Not needed at runtime.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
pgdata/
*.bak
_to_delete/
error.txt

# The pipeline's own application code. The signer deliberately shares only the
# two dependency-free modules its Dockerfile names explicitly; everything else
# belongs to the web image and must not be in this one.
main.py
engine.py
paper_trading.py
market_data.py
free_market_data.py
token_discovery.py
gmgn_market_data.py
gmgn_diagnose.py
app_time.py
probe_*.py
explore_*.py
smoke_test_*.py
test_provider_access.py
tests/
